Decision rules
  D1: G1 (weak form) and the gate hold with the unrounded c* (60/60) -> the rounding of c* to two decimals explains the misses of P7; R1 NOT TRUSTED is lifted for the B column (Bn control reproduced: True).  c*_AM2(128) = -2.9763 is farther than 0.10 from -2.40 -> droplet_ctrl_am2's AM2 columns must be rerun with the recalibrated c* before being quoted.  A prereg that prints power tables to the digit must quote c* to four decimals.
  D2: |c*_B(480) - c*_B(128)| = 0.1857 -> <= 0.25: a c* tied to the control count is not forced by this calibration.  |c*_AM2(480) - c*_B(480)| = 0.7782 -> > 0.05: AM2 needs its own c*.  c*_B(480) = -2.0198, c*_AM2(480) = -2.7980; calibration values only (no false STEP or power evaluated at 480).
  D3: P_A <= 0.50 in 15/18 cells and P_B >= 0.75 in 8/9 low-misread cells -> AM2 gives up most of the ability to reject a sharp step in smooth Bak-like data; adopting AM2 means the prereg can no longer claim that a SMOOTH label rejects a sharp step (only 'smooth, or a step with a plateau'), to be weighed against B's plateau blind spot.
  D4: no sharp-truth share above 0.15 for either rule.
  D5: nothing is edited in journals/droplet_prereg.md or any existing file; all wording is marked NOT APPLIED.
